From: Fabiano Tassotti <fabianotassotti@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: realtek: add opt-in RTL8367D switch support

Add the RTL8367S-VB/RTL8367D switch and VLAN pipeline implementation, including correct transitions between standalone and VLAN-aware operation. All behavior is gated by explicit firmware properties.

The RTL8367D register layouts and legacy initialization behavior are based
on OpenWrt's GPL-2.0 rtl8367b driver, originally written by Gabor Juhos and
later extended for RTL8367D by Mieczyslaw Nalewaj and Serge Vasilugin:

Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/blob/main/target/linux/generic/files/drivers/net/phy/rtl8367b.c
Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/14804

The DSA integration, per-switch opt-ins, VLAN transitions and compatibility
fallbacks were implemented and adapted for the MR80X v5 by Fabiano Tassotti.

Signed-off-by: Fabiano Tassotti <fabianotassotti@gmail.com>

diff --git a/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_l2.c b/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_l2.c
index 0494d8a..48dde4c 100644
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_l2.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/realtek/rtl8365mb_l2.c
@@ -381,6 +381,34 @@ int rtl8365mb_l2_del_uc(struct realtek_priv *priv, int port,
 	return ret;
 }
 
+int rtl8365mb_l2_reset(struct realtek_priv *priv)
+{
+	u32 val;
+	int ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * Boot firmware may leave the LUT full of static entries. A per-port
+	 * dynamic flush cannot remove those entries, so reset the entire table
+	 * before DSA starts installing bridge FDB entries.
+	 */
+	mutex_lock(&priv->map_lock);
+
+	ret = regmap_write(priv->map_nolock, RTL8365MB_L2_FLUSH_CTRL3_REG,
+			   FIELD_PREP(RTL8365MB_L2_FLUSH_CTRL3_MSK, 1));
+	if (ret)
+		goto out;
+
+	ret = regmap_read_poll_timeout(priv->map_nolock,
+				       RTL8365MB_L2_FLUSH_CTRL3_REG,
+				       val,
+				       !(val & RTL8365MB_L2_FLUSH_CTRL3_MSK),
+				       10, 10000);
+out:
+	mutex_unlock(&priv->map_lock);
+
+	return ret;
+}
+
 int rtl8365mb_l2_flush(struct realtek_priv *priv, int port, u16 vid)
 {
 	int mode = vid ? RTL8365MB_L2_FLUSH_CTRL2_MODE_PORT_VID :
